    # Baiocassium (Chapter Three: Hermetic History and Culture, Past and Present Covenants, p28): a covenant of the Tribunal’s past, from its register entry.

    #tc29e9f869622a90fb12d21 ^"Baiocassium" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tMql8hzM4bv6ng0WYA6N9VrH ^"Covenant"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Years" STRING "851 – 1011"
            ^"Liege" LIST [#t4c5cfade6ecf08fadc1b28 ^"Branugurix"]
            ^"Vassals" LIST [#ta7283fa2993fe4ca204d53 ^"Baiocassium Minor"]
            ^"Register Entry" STRING "Baiocassium (851 – 1011): Vassal of Branugurix, located in the forest near Bayeux. The magi of Baiocassium, predominantly of House Diedne, were the descendants of Gallic druids and had good relationships with the local faeries."
